Commands and events become submodules. A command with params and returns gets
params + result records; a zero-return command gets result = unit; an event
gets params and its wire name.

  $ cat > browser.json << 'EOF'
  > {"domains":[{"domain":"Demo","commands":[
  >   {"name":"getItem","parameters":[
  >     {"name":"itemId","type":"string"}
  >   ],"returns":[
  >     {"name":"found","type":"boolean"}
  >   ]},
  >   {"name":"reset"}
  > ],"events":[
  >   {"name":"itemChanged","parameters":[
  >     {"name":"itemId","type":"string"}
  >   ]}
  > ]}]}
  > EOF
  $ echo '{"domains":[]}' > js.json
  $ mkdir out && cdp-gen generate browser.json js.json out Demo
  generated cdp_base.ml: 0 sealed alias modules
  generated cdp_demo(_types).ml: 0 types, 2 commands, 1 events
  generated cdp.ml index (1 domains, protocol unknown)
  $ cat out/cdp_demo.ml
